Q) : my docker image is size is 1GB , now how i can reduce size of the image ?

A): 
 1. Use minimal base images like alpine or slim to start with a smaller footprint.
 2. Implement multi-stage builds to separate the build environment from the final image, copying only the necessary artifacts.
 3. Clean up package manager caches and temporary files to avoid leftover data increasing image size.
 4. Combine multiple RUN commands into a single layer to reduce the number of image layers.
 5. Use a .dockerignore file and strip binaries (for compiled apps) to exclude unnecessary files and reduce binary sizes.
